From: AOSC OS Packaging <packages@aosc.io>
Subject: [PATCH] Make the C_LOOP configuration compile

Two fixes for building this fork with -DENABLE_C_LOOP=ON (any architecture
without a JSC MacroAssembler backend, e.g. loongarch64; reproducible on
x86_64 by forcing the option):

- DFGAbstractHeap.h: hoist the plain AbstractHeapKind enum out of
  ENABLE(DFG_JIT).  Bun extends DOMJIT::Effect with AbstractHeapKind
  read/write metadata (DOMJITEffect.h), so the type must exist even when
  the DFG itself is compiled out; the enum depends on nothing else.
- JSModuleLoader.cpp: include <wtf/Scope.h> explicitly for makeScopeExit;
  under C_LOOP it is no longer pulled in transitively.

Verified on x86_64: -DENABLE_JIT=OFF -DENABLE_C_LOOP=ON with all of Bun's
options builds cleanly and the resulting jsc passes a smoke test (with
WebAssembly correctly absent).

Signed-off-by: AOSC OS Packaging <packages@aosc.io>
---
